---

<Layout>
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <figure class="hero-art reveal in">
        <img src="/images/hero-kaaba.webp" alt="Illustration of the Kaaba in Makkah at dusk" width="1200" height="480" fetchpriority="high" />
      </figure>
      <h1 id="page-title">Umrah Package Calculator Pakistan</h1>
      <p class="lede">Estimate your Umrah package cost in <strong>PKR</strong> — pick your departure city, duration, hotel tier and sharing, and get an instant per-person and total estimate with a full price breakdown. Built for Pakistani pilgrims, free forever, no signup.</p>
      <ul class="trust" aria-label="Why use this calculator">
        <li>Prices in Pakistani Rupees</li>
        <li>8 departure cities covered</li>
        <li>Full cost breakdown shown</li>
        <li>100% private — nothing uploaded</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Calculator />

  <div class="wrap">
    <section id="how-to-use" class="how-band reveal" aria-labelledby="how-to-use-h">
      <h2 id="how-to-use-h">How to Use This Calculator</h2>
      <p class="sub">Four steps, under a minute — all prices in PKR.</p>
      <figure class="how-fig">
        <img src="/images/how-to-use.webp" alt="Four-step illustration: choose city, pick hotel and sharing, select travel month, get PKR price breakdown" width="900" height="420" loading="lazy" />
      </figure>
      <div class="steps-grid">
        <div class="step-card">
          <span class="step-num">1</span>
          <h3>Choose your city</h3>
          <p>Select your <strong>departure city</strong> in Pakistan — Karachi, Lahore, Islamabad and 5 more. Flight costs adjust automatically.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-card">
          <span class="step-num">2</span>
          <h3>Pick duration &amp; hotels</h3>
          <p>Choose <strong>7–28 days</strong>, a hotel tier (Economy 3★ → Luxury 5★), and room sharing (quad is cheapest).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-card">
          <span class="step-num">3</span>
          <h3>Set season &amp; travelers</h3>
          <p>Pick your <strong>travel season</strong> — Ramadan costs far more than summer — and add adults and children.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-card">
          <span class="step-num">4</span>
          <h3>Get your estimate</h3>
          <p>See the <strong>total in PKR</strong> with an animated per-component breakdown: flights, hotels, visa, transport, ziarat.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap">
  <article class="article" aria-label="Complete guide to Umrah package costs from Pakistan">

    <nav class="toc reveal" aria-label="Guide contents">
      <h2>In this guide</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#how-to-use">How to use this calculator</a></li>
        <li><a href="#included">What an Umrah package includes</a></li>
        <li><a href="#prices">Umrah package prices in Pakistan 2026</a></li>
        <li><a href="#methodology">How this calculator estimates your cost</a></li>
        <li><a href="#cities">Departure cities: where to fly from</a></li>
        <li><a href="#seasons">Best time to go: seasons &amp; prices</a></li>
        <li><a href="#hotels">Hotel tiers explained</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sharing">Room sharing: quad vs triple vs double</a></li>
        <li><a href="#save">9 ways to save money on Umrah</a></li>
        <li><a href="#licensed">Choosing a licensed operator</a></li>
        <li><a href="#faq">Frequently asked questions</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <div class="est-note reveal"><strong>Indicative estimates.</strong> Prices below are compiled from published 2026 Umrah package rates in Pakistan and are typically within 10–15% of operator quotes. Airline seats, hotel availability, and the PKR–SAR exchange rate move constantly — always confirm with a licensed operator before paying.</div>

    <section id="included" class="reveal" aria-labelledby="included-h">
      <h2 id="included-h">What an Umrah Package Includes</h2>
      <p>A standard Umrah package from Pakistan bundles five things. Understanding each one is the key to reading any quote — and to knowing where your money actually goes.</p>
      <figure>
        <img src="/images/price-breakdown.webp" alt="Illustration of Umrah cost breakdown: flights, hotels, visa, transport and ziarat" width="800" height="500" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>The five building blocks of every Umrah package price.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <h3>1. Visa and insurance</h3>
      <p>The Umrah visa (or Saudi tourist e-visa used for Umrah) plus mandatory travel insurance. Budget around <strong>PKR 40,000–50,000</strong> per person. This is the one component with almost no variation between operators.</p>
      <h3>2. Return flights</h3>
      <p>Usually the single biggest cost: roughly <strong>PKR 108,000–219,000</strong> return in economy depending on city, airline, and season. PIA, Saudia, Airblue, Serene Air, and Fly Jinnah operate direct routes from Karachi, Lahore, and Islamabad; other cities often connect through these hubs or the Gulf.</p>
      <h3>3. Hotels in Makkah and Madinah</h3>
      <p>The most variable component. A 3-star room a shuttle ride from the Haram costs a fraction of a 5-star room overlooking it. Packages quote per-person prices on a sharing basis — quad sharing divides one room's cost four ways.</p>
      <h3>4. Ground transport</h3>
      <p>Airport pickups, Jeddah–Makkah–Madinah transfers (by bus or the Haramain high-speed train on premium packages), and private vs. shared vehicles. Budget options share a bus; luxury options include private cars.</p>
      <h3>5. Ziarat and on-ground services</h3>
      <p>Guided visits to historical sites — Jabal al-Noor, Jabal Thawr, Masjid Quba, Mount Uhud — plus a group guide, SIM assistance, and sometimes Zamzam. Economy packages cover the basics; premium ones add private guides.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="prices" class="reveal" aria-labelledby="prices-h">
      <h2 id="prices-h">Umrah Package Prices in Pakistan 2026</h2>
      <p>Here is what Pakistani operators are actually advertising for the 2026 season. These are per-person, quad-sharing baselines — use the calculator above for your exact combination.</p>
      <table class="price-table">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Duration</th><th scope="col">Economy (3★)</th><th scope="col">Standard (4★)</th><th scope="col">Luxury (5★)</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>7 days</td><td>PKR 158,000</td><td>PKR 230,000–280,000</td><td>PKR 550,000+</td></tr>
          <tr><td>10 days</td><td>PKR 198,000</td><td>PKR 280,000–380,000</td><td>PKR 600,000+</td></tr>
          <tr><td>14 days</td><td>PKR 245,000–255,000</td><td>PKR 305,000–410,000</td><td>PKR 598,000–720,000</td></tr>
          <tr><td>21 days</td><td>PKR 310,000</td><td>PKR 400,000–480,000</td><td>PKR 750,000+</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>Two patterns jump out. First, the <strong>14-day package is the sweet spot</strong> Pakistani families book most: two weeks in the Haramain, two Jumuah prayers, unhurried ziarat. Second, the jump from 4-star to 5-star is far bigger than from 3-star to 4-star — you are paying for meters from the Haram, not just stars.</p>
      <p>Note that some advertised prices exclude airfare (always check the fine print). The calculator above <em>includes</em> estimated return flights from your city, so its totals run higher than "visa + hotel only" quotes — that is intentional and more honest.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="methodology" class="reveal" aria-labelledby="methodology-h">
      <h2 id="methodology-h">How This Calculator Estimates Your Cost</h2>
      <p>No black box here — the full method, so you can judge the number:</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Visa + insurance:</strong> flat PKR 42,000 per person.</li>
        <li><strong>Flights:</strong> city-specific return estimates (Karachi PKR 135,000 up to Quetta PKR 170,000), based on 2026 economy fares on PIA, Saudia, and private carriers.</li>
        <li><strong>Hotels:</strong> per-night, per-person rates for your tier and cities of stay (e.g., 14 days = 9 nights Makkah + 5 nights Madinah), multiplied by a sharing factor — quad ×1.0, triple ×1.25, double ×1.7.</li>
        <li><strong>Transport + ziarat/services:</strong> tier-based flat amounts (shared bus on economy, private vehicles on luxury).</li>
        <li><strong>Season multiplier:</strong> Ramadan ×1.45, December–January ×1.15, Rabi-ul-Awwal ×1.10, June–August ×0.95, other months ×1.0.</li>
        <li><strong>Children (2–11):</strong> 65% of the adult total; infants excluded.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Totals are rounded to the nearest PKR 500. Treat the result as a planning figure within about 10–15% of real quotes — close enough to budget, choose a tier, and compare operators, but not a substitute for a written quotation.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="cities" class="reveal" aria-labelledby="cities-h">
      <h2 id="cities-h">Departure Cities: Where to Fly From</h2>
      <p>Your Pakistani departure city moves the price more than most people expect — up to PKR 35,000 per person between the cheapest and priciest airports.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Karachi</strong> — usually cheapest. Most airline options, most competition, frequent Umrah departures. If you live in Sindh, this is your default.</li>
        <li><strong>Lahore</strong> — slightly above Karachi, but the best choice for Punjab families with frequent group departures and strong availability.</li>
        <li><strong>Islamabad</strong> — comparable to Lahore; the natural hub for northern Punjab, KPK, and Azad Kashmir travelers (Rawalpindi pricing overlaps).</li>
        <li><strong>Faisalabad / Sialkot / Multan</strong> — mid-range; often routed via Lahore or attached to group blocks. Convenient if you live nearby, rarely the cheapest.</li>
        <li><strong>Peshawar</strong> — higher, driven by routing and seasonal seat supply. KPK travelers sometimes save by departing from Islamabad instead.</li>
        <li><strong>Quetta</strong> — typically the priciest, with the fewest direct options.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Practical tip: if two airports are within driving distance, price both. A family of four can save over a lakh by departing from Karachi instead of Quetta — easily worth a domestic hop.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="seasons" class="reveal" aria-labelledby="seasons-h">
      <h2 id="seasons-h">Best Time to Go: Seasons &amp; Prices</h2>
      <p>When you travel matters almost as much as how long you stay:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Ramadan (especially the last 10 nights):</strong> the most rewarding and the most expensive — expect 40–60% above normal months. Book 4–6 months ahead; hotels near the Haram sell out.</li>
        <li><strong>December–January:</strong> winter rush. Pleasant weather in Saudi Arabia pulls huge Pakistani crowds; prices run ~15% high. Book 2–3 months ahead.</li>
        <li><strong>Rabi-ul-Awwal:</strong> a mini-peak around the Prophet's ﷺ birthday; ~10% premium, festive atmosphere in Madinah.</li>
        <li><strong>June–August:</strong> the value season. Brutal heat keeps crowds (and prices) down — about 5% cheaper, with emptier mataf areas. Not for the elderly or those sensitive to heat.</li>
        <li><strong>Shoulder months (Feb–May, Sep–Nov):</strong> the balanced choice — moderate weather, moderate prices, moderate crowds.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="hotels" class="reveal" aria-labelledby="hotels-h">
      <h2 id="hotels-h">Hotel Tiers Explained</h2>
      <figure>
        <img src="/images/hotel-tiers.webp" alt="Illustration of 3-star, 4-star and 5-star hotels near the Haram" width="800" height="500" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>What the stars really buy: distance from the Haram.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p>The star rating on an Umrah package is mostly a proxy for one thing: <strong>walking distance to the Haram</strong>.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Economy (3★):</strong> typically 700m–1.5km away, often with shuttle buses. Clean and functional; you will walk or ride for every prayer. Best for the budget-conscious and the young.</li>
        <li><strong>Standard (4★):</strong> roughly 200–400m away — walkable in minutes. The best value for most Pakistani families, especially with elderly parents.</li>
        <li><strong>Luxury (5★):</strong> 50–200m, sometimes with Haram or Kaaba views, premium dining and service. You pay several lakhs extra for those meters.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>For elderly pilgrims or anyone with mobility issues, hotel distance is the single most important "luxury" — more than room size or food. A 4-star at 250 meters beats a 5-star at 600 meters for tired feet.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="sharing" class="reveal" aria-labelledby="sharing-h">
      <h2 id="sharing-h">Room Sharing: Quad vs Triple vs Double</h2>
      <p>Pakistani Umrah packages quote per-person prices on a sharing basis, and this choice swings the total dramatically:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Quad (4 persons):</strong> the baseline and cheapest — one room's cost split four ways. Standard for budget and family groups.</li>
        <li><strong>Triple (3 persons):</strong> about 25% more per person. Noticeably more comfortable, still economical.</li>
        <li><strong>Double (2 persons):</strong> about 70% more per person. The choice for couples and those who value privacy and rest.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Try it in the calculator: switch a 14-day standard package from quad to double and watch the per-person price jump. Families often mix — quad for the group, one double room for elderly parents.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="save" class="reveal" aria-labelledby="save-h">
      <h2 id="save-h">9 Ways to Save Money on Umrah</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Travel off-peak.</strong> June–August or shoulder months beat Ramadan and winter by 20–50%.</li>
        <li><strong>Choose quad sharing.</strong> The single biggest lever on per-person cost.</li>
        <li><strong>Pick the 10-day package.</strong> Most families' sweet spot — all the essentials, three fewer hotel nights than 14 days.</li>
        <li><strong>Depart from Karachi or Lahore</strong> if feasible — cheaper flights than Peshawar or Quetta.</li>
        <li><strong>Book 2–3 months early</strong> (4–6 for Ramadan) to lock cheaper airline seats.</li>
        <li><strong>Compare 3+ licensed operators</strong> with written, itemized quotations — never a verbal price.</li>
        <li><strong>Travel in a group.</strong> Operators discount group blocks; family packages of 4+ often save up to 15%.</li>
        <li><strong>Skip the 5-star unless you need it.</strong> A 4-star 250m from the Haram beats a distant 5-star for most pilgrims.</li>
        <li><strong>Watch the exchange rate.</strong> Packages are costed in Saudi Riyals; a weaker rupee quietly inflates every quote.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section id="licensed" class="reveal" aria-labelledby="licensed-h">
      <h2 id="licensed-h">Choosing a Licensed Operator</h2>
      <p>Pakistan regulates Umrah travel: operators must be licensed by the Ministry of Religious Affairs. This is your main protection against fraud, and it is worth five minutes of checking:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Verify the agency's license on the Ministry of Religious Affairs website or helpline before paying anything.</li>
        <li>Insist on a <strong>written, itemized quotation</strong>: visa, flights (with airline and dates), hotel names (not just "3-star"), distances from the Haram, transport type, and ziarat inclusions.</li>
        <li>Never pay the full amount upfront to an unverified agent; licensed operators issue proper receipts.</li>
        <li>Be skeptical of prices far below market — the classic sign of a scam or of brutal hidden downgrades (a "3-star" 3km away with no shuttle).</li>
        <li>Ask for the hotel booking confirmations before departure, and save the operator's 24/7 contact for Saudi Arabia.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="faq" class="reveal" aria-labelledby="faq-h">
      <h2 id="faq-h">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <details class="faq-item" open>
        <summary>How accurate is this Umrah package calculator?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>It is an indicative estimate built from published 2026 package prices in Pakistan, typically within 10–15% of operator quotes for the same inputs. Actual prices move with airline seats, hotel availability, and the PKR–SAR exchange rate, so always confirm with a licensed operator before paying.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Does the estimate include return airfare from Pakistan?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. The calculator includes estimated return economy airfare from your selected Pakistani departure city — Karachi, Lahore, Islamabad, Faisalabad, Sialkot, Multan, Peshawar, or Quetta.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Why are Ramadan Umrah packages so much more expensive?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>Demand peaks in Ramadan, especially the last ten nights, so airlines and hotels near the Haram raise prices sharply — often 40–60% above normal months. The calculator applies a Ramadan multiplier to reflect this.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Which departure city in Pakistan is cheapest for Umrah?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>Karachi is usually cheapest thanks to more airline options and competition, followed by Lahore and Islamabad. Peshawar and Quetta tend to cost more because of routing and fewer direct seats.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>How much does room sharing affect the price?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>A lot. Quad sharing (4 persons per room) is the baseline and cheapest. Triple sharing typically costs about 25% more per person, and double sharing about 70% more, because the same room cost is split fewer ways.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Are children charged the full package price?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>Not usually. Children aged 2–11 sharing a bed with parents are typically charged around 65% of the adult price, which is what this calculator uses. Infants under 2 usually pay only visa and airline charges — confirm with your operator.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>What is the real difference between 3-star and 5-star Umrah packages?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>Mostly distance from the Haram and comfort. Economy 3-star hotels are often 700m–1.5km away with shuttle buses; 4-star hotels sit 200–400m away; 5-star hotels are 50–200m from the Haram with premium service. The rituals are identical — you are paying for proximity and comfort.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Should I book through an agent or arrange Umrah myself?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>Pakistan requires Umrah travel through government-licensed operators for visa processing in most cases. A licensed agent bundles visa, flights, hotels, and transport — and is accountable if something goes wrong. DIY booking suits experienced travelers but leaves you handling every problem alone.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>How early should I book my Umrah package?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>Book 2–3 months ahead for normal months and 4–6 months ahead for Ramadan or December–January. Early booking locks in cheaper airline seats and better hotel choices near the Haram.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Is this calculator affiliated with any travel agency?</summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>No. It is an independent estimate tool. It does not sell packages, collect your data, or earn commission from any operator — the numbers are computed in your browser from published market prices.</p></div>
      </details>
    </section>

    <section id="conclusion" class="reveal" aria-labelledby="conclusion-h">
      <h2 id="conclusion-h">Plan Smart, Travel Blessed</h2>
      <p>Umrah is a journey of the heart — but it is also a major household expense, and Pakistani families deserve honest numbers before they commit. Use the calculator to find the combination that fits your budget, compare two or three licensed operators with itemized quotes, and book early. May your journey be accepted.</p>
      <div class="cta-band">
        <h2>Estimate your Umrah cost</h2>
        <p>Free forever. No signup. All prices in PKR.</p>
        <a class="btn" href="#tool">Open the calculator</a>
      </div>
      <p style="font-size:.82rem;color:var(--muted)">Last updated: October 2026 · Indicative estimates only — not a travel agency.</p>
    </section>

  </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
